THOUGHT: NullAway complains because IntMap.get may return null, and beforeGroup dereferences it without a null check. afterGroup already handles a possible null plug. To mirror that and avoid changing behavior, I should add a local variable, check for null, and only call beforeGroup if non-null. Then I must run the Gradle compile to confirm the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '31,33c\  @Override
  public void beforeGroup(int group, Array<Decal> contents) {
    GroupPlug plug = plugs.get(group);
    if (plug != null) {
      plug.beforeGroup(contents);
    }
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/decals/PluggableGroupStrategy.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "PluggableGroupStrategy" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

